[ I am reposting this message because I have an update to add:  Some people
have reported having trouble accessing the Project Armageddon Website.  The
reason for this problem is that our server (Geocities) handles a large
volume and during certain times of the day it can be hard to access the
sites they host (which we are one of).   If this problem occurs when you
try to access our website -- please try again later, or just email me and
ask me to send you all of the information. ]

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--------------------------------------------

Hi there.  I am writing this message to tell you about Project Armageddon. 
"What is it?" you may ask.

It is a project to develop a freeware DirectX strategy game (in the style
of Warcraft II.)  I have great plans for this game.  But, to turn these
plans into an actual game -- I'm going to need some assistance.  At the
moment its just me.  (I have begun designing the game, and at the same time
diving into the intracies of DirectX code.)

I'm looking for games developers and designers, artists, sound (Digitized
Sound and/or MIDI) composers, and anyone else who would like to help out. 
The game is going to be freeware, so I'm not hiring anyone -- I'm looking
for volunteers.

I have created a website for Project Armageddon and placed a good bit of
information on it.  If you are interested, or curiousity simply has the
better of you I strongly suggest you check out the website.  Its at:

http://www.geocities.com/SiliconValley/Park/8875

If you aren't interested or don't have the time, please pass the word to
your friends.  If you have a website, you could do me a big favor by
placing a link to my site on your page.  (Let me know if you do, I'll put
up a link to your site.)

If you have any questions or comments, you can reach me by e-mail at
Porchmonkey@Juno.com

Thanks,
Peter DeLaurentis
<Porchmonkey@Juno.com>
"Let Armageddon begin!!!"


